  "name": "process-panexperientialism",
  "title": "Process Panexperientialism",
  "role": "model",
  "summary": "Process panexperientialism, from Alfred North Whitehead and David Ray Griffin: the final realities are momentary actual occasions of experience, each a concrescence of prehensions of past occasions into one new unity that perishes into a datum for the next. Experience is everywhere, consciousness is a rare late form of it, and mind and body are routes of such occasions.",
